WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.380
Hi, I'm Hyacinth!

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:06.375
ORPO trains on preferred and rejected answers in a single run.

00:00:06.375 --> 00:00:08.917
Here's how its one extra term works.

00:00:10.517 --> 00:00:14.820
The idea: fine-tuning on chosen answers lifts the rejected ones too.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:20.296
ORPO adds a term that pushes the rejected answer down, with no reference model.

00:00:21.817 --> 00:00:23.345
The whole method is one line.

00:00:23.817 --> 00:00:26.391
The usual SFT loss on the chosen answer.

00:00:26.391 --> 00:00:27.677
It never switches off.

00:00:28.097 --> 00:00:32.794
A penalty that shrinks as the chosen answer's odds rise above the rejected one's.

00:00:33.214 --> 00:00:34.462
Lambda sets its weight.

00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:39.254
What goes into the odds?

00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:45.770
P is the average per-token probability, a geometric mean, not the whole sequence's probability.

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:48.388
That keeps P where one minus P matters.

00:00:48.388 --> 00:00:51.135
For a whole sequence, the odds would just equal P.

00:00:52.442 --> 00:00:56.213
With a probability ratio at beta point two, reaching a loss of

00:00:56.213 --> 00:00:59.355
point zero one means all but erasing the rejected answer.

00:00:59.775 --> 00:01:03.424
The odds ratio spreads over nine times wider, so the rejected answer

00:01:03.424 --> 00:01:06.769
only has to fall to about one and a half percent.

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:09.677
The gradient has a gate.

00:01:09.677 --> 00:01:13.438
On pairs the model already gets right, ORPO is just SFT.

00:01:13.438 --> 00:01:17.199
When it prefers the rejected answer, the pull is two hundred

00:01:17.199 --> 00:01:18.566
and forty times stronger.

00:01:19.842 --> 00:01:24.473
And a result the paper never reported: in another group's matched runs,

00:01:24.473 --> 00:01:29.105
ORPO raised GSM8K math by two and a half points on average.

00:01:29.105 --> 00:01:30.649
DPO lost over eight.

00:01:31.767 --> 00:01:35.936
Keep the SFT term live on every step, and preference training stops

00:01:35.936 --> 00:01:37.325
eating the model's arithmetic.

00:01:39.317 --> 00:01:43.730
To recap: SFT plus an odds-ratio penalty, averaged per token, that only

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:45.936
bites where the model is wrong.

00:01:46.356 --> 00:01:48.518
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:48.518 --> 00:01:49.136
I'm Hyacinth.

00:01:49.136 --> 00:01:49.445
Bye!
